WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.701
-Come on, bud.
It's always good to see you.

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:04.701
I have lots of things
to talk to you about.

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:08.334
-First of all, let me thank you
for being so nice to my wife

00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:09.834
-Your wife?
-when she was here.

00:00:09.834 --> 00:00:11.534
-She was so funny.
-That's like one

00:00:11.534 --> 00:00:13.634
of the best shows
I've ever seen you do.

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:14.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:16.467
-It was.
It was good.

00:00:16.467 --> 00:00:18.100
She was fantastic.
She was on fire, by the way.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.834
Tell her to come back
whenever she wants.

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:21.000
-Yeah.
-She crushed. I love her.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.434
-Thank you.
-And we'll talk about her

00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:23.667
later on,
when we talk about the play.

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:26.300
-Okay.
-Now, I want to talk
about Nick Fury.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:27.267
-Oh.
-Yes!

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:28.801
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:28.801 --> 00:00:29.868
Fans are waiting.

00:00:29.868 --> 00:00:31.267
I'm waiting.

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:33.200
Two new Marvel projects --

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.734
"The Marvels"
and "Secret Invasion."

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:38.067
Are you excited
to play him again?

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:40.934
-Always excited to, you know,
put that eyepatch on

00:00:40.934 --> 00:00:44.300
or just hang out with some
of the people that I really,

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.767
really enjoy being
around when that's happening.

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:50.634
Like Brie is like amazing
and the whole new setup

00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:53.934
with the Marvels,
the new family.

00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:54.667
-You like getting in there.

00:00:54.667 --> 00:00:57.067
I saw you just you made

00:00:57.067 --> 00:00:58.501
an appearance
on "Sesame Street."

00:00:58.501 --> 00:01:00.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.467 --> 00:01:01.334
Not the Avengers.

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:02.667
This is the...
-Aveggies.

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:04.100
-...Aveggies.
-Yeah!

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:05.701
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah. And these are
the Aveggies.

00:01:05.701 --> 00:01:06.868
[ Applause ]

00:01:06.868 --> 00:01:08.033
[ Cheering ]

00:01:08.033 --> 00:01:09.267
-Come on, bud.

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:10.834
That's why we love you.
Come on.

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:12.667
You do -- Come on,
that's cool, that you do that.

00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:14.033
-A bucket list thing.

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:16.300
I've been trying to get
on "Sesame Street" for years.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.901
[ Laughter ]
-Is that right?
-Oh, yeah, yeah.

00:01:17.901 --> 00:01:21.267
I've been after my publicist
and all my people like,

00:01:21.267 --> 00:01:22.567
"When am I going
to get on 'Sesame Street'?"

00:01:22.567 --> 00:01:25.601
And every time I see
somebody else on there, I go,

00:01:25.601 --> 00:01:26.968
"How'd they get on there and I'm

00:01:26.968 --> 00:01:28.234
[ Laughter ]
still not on 'Sesame Street'?"

00:01:28.234 --> 00:01:30.000
-Yeah. I mean, well, I mean,
you've probably had

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.067
to watch your mouth a little bit
around the Muppets.

00:01:32.067 --> 00:01:33.868
-Every now and then.
The word of the day couldn't be

00:01:33.868 --> 00:01:35.133
my favorite word,
that's for sure.

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:37.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:39.734
-I read this interesting fact
about you.

00:01:39.734 --> 00:01:41.300
That, when you were
doing "Star Wars,"

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.100
that you used to carry
a lightsaber around

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:44.567
in your golf bag.

00:01:44.567 --> 00:01:48.033
-Episode...III, yeah.

00:01:48.033 --> 00:01:51.367
-So you could practice doing --
-Well, I had my practice
lightsaber.

00:01:51.367 --> 00:01:53.300
Well, actually,
it was the lightsaber

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:56.467
that I actually used
to actually fight in the film

00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:59.033
because you actually have like
a saber that has

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:01.767
like a plastic metal thing
that's covered in plastic.

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:03.968
So, it has all kinds
of nicks and --

00:02:03.968 --> 00:02:06.067
-Really? For rehearsing?
-Yeah, from rehearsing.

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:11.801
But I had like a 93- to 98-move
thing to learn...

00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:14.033
-Yeah.
-...going through three rooms,

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.033
mostly backwards, so...

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:18.534
-Yeah, I guess so, yeah.
-when I was --

00:02:18.534 --> 00:02:20.934
had downtime in the tee box,
standing around,

00:02:20.934 --> 00:02:23.100
I would just take it out
and go through my head

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.501
[ Laughter ]
like I was going through,
doing stuff,

00:02:25.501 --> 00:02:27.601
but, you know,
and I would do it.

00:02:27.601 --> 00:02:28.868
-Yeah. And people
were cool with that?

00:02:28.868 --> 00:02:29.767
-Oh, yeah, yeah.

00:02:29.767 --> 00:02:30.968
[ Laughter ]
-They're like,

00:02:30.968 --> 00:02:32.033
"That's fun"?
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:33.334
The people I was playing with,
you know,

00:02:33.334 --> 00:02:35.501
they knew what was happening,
so, it was alright.

00:02:35.501 --> 00:02:36.701
[ Laughter ]
-Mace Windu's just going

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:37.934
for it, yeah.
-Yeah, man, just go in there,

00:02:37.934 --> 00:02:40.200
doing my thing.
It's not simple.

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.100
-I have a --
-Oh, look out.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:45.334
[ Cheering and applause ]
Ah ah ah.

00:02:45.334 --> 00:02:46.901
Y...eah.

00:02:46.901 --> 00:02:48.167
-I have one for me, too.

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:49.000
I'm feeling that.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:50.100
[ Humming ]

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:50.767
[ Whoosh ]

00:02:50.767 --> 00:02:52.634
[ Oohs ]
Whoa!

00:02:52.634 --> 00:02:53.767
-How'd you do that?

00:02:53.767 --> 00:02:54.968
-I used the Force.

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:57.734
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, no.

00:02:57.734 --> 00:02:59.367
-You know something
I don't know.

00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:00.501
-Can we dim the lights?

00:03:00.734 --> 00:03:02.667
[ Laughter ]
-Boop it again.

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:04.033
-Yeah, can you boop it again?
-Boop!

00:03:04.033 --> 00:03:07.634
[ Hissing, humming ]
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:07.634 --> 00:03:08.834
-Alright, now. Ooh!

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:10.100
Now, what do we do?

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:12.033
Wow, that's good, right --
That feels cool there.

00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:14.868
-But do they make clashing
sounds when they hit?

00:03:14.868 --> 00:03:15.801
[ The Roots playing
suspenseful rock ]
[ Whooshing ]

00:03:15.801 --> 00:03:16.467
-Oh, they do.

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:17.934
[ Whooshing ]

00:03:17.934 --> 00:03:19.000
Mine does.
-Little bit.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:19.834
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:03:19.834 --> 00:03:20.667
This one does.

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:21.634
-[Indistinct]

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:22.901
[ Whooshing ]

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:23.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.567 --> 00:03:24.467
What you got?

00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:25.434
What you got? What you got?

00:03:25.434 --> 00:03:27.801
[ Cheering ]

00:03:27.801 --> 00:03:28.901
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:28.901 --> 00:03:37.434
♪♪

00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:43.501
♪♪

00:03:43.501 --> 00:03:44.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.834 --> 00:03:48.267
[ Cheering and applause ]
[ Rimshot ]

00:03:48.267 --> 00:03:50.067
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:50.067 --> 00:03:50.934
Come on.

00:03:50.934 --> 00:03:52.234
-Now, will it just stay purple?

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:54.000
-Yeah, no, yeah, just stay on.
Here we go.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.033
-Uh!

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:56.767
[ Whoosh ]
-Thank you. Wow.

00:03:56.767 --> 00:03:59.200
[ Laughter ]
-Getting that for Christmas.
-Thank you for doing it. I know.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.300
-My pleasure. My pleasure.
-I can't wait. Thank you, buddy.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:02.968
Can we talk about "The Piano
Lesson," please?

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:04.000
-Yes, please.

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:05.801
-This is at the
Barrymore Theatre.

00:04:05.801 --> 00:04:08.000
-Ah!
-You're getting
rave reviews on this

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.601
and you're directed by your

00:04:09.601 --> 00:04:10.667
very talented wife.
-My wife, LaTanya,

00:04:10.667 --> 00:04:11.767
directed it, yes.

00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:14.300
And we're having a measure
of success,

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:16.033
to the point that we've been
extended, now,

00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:17.767
till January 29th!

00:04:17.767 --> 00:04:18.801
-That's what I'm talking about!

00:04:18.801 --> 00:04:22.534
[ Cheering and applause ]
[ Rimshot ]

00:04:22.534 --> 00:04:23.934
-So.

00:04:23.934 --> 00:04:25.367
-Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:04:25.367 --> 00:04:27.334
So, if you're doing nothing
over the holidays,

00:04:27.334 --> 00:04:28.801
come see the show or...

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:30.200
-Yeah.
-Christmas night.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.367
We have a show Christmas night.

00:04:31.367 --> 00:04:32.868
-You're working on Christmas?

00:04:32.868 --> 00:04:35.000
-8:00 Christmas night.
-No way!

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:36.234
-Yeah.
-You really got to work

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:37.567
over there on Broadway, man.
-Mm-hmm.

00:04:37.567 --> 00:04:40.033
-Can we say
what the play's about?

00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:41.567
Can we we set it up?

00:04:41.567 --> 00:04:43.367
-Wow.
It's a play --

00:04:43.367 --> 00:04:48.467
"The Piano Lesson" is
about an heirloom piano that's

00:04:48.467 --> 00:04:50.701
in the house in Pittsburgh

00:04:50.701 --> 00:04:55.434
that Berniece, my niece,
cherishes.

00:04:55.434 --> 00:04:56.834
It's a family heirloom.

00:04:56.834 --> 00:04:58.834
And her brother, Boy Willie,

00:04:58.834 --> 00:05:01.567
played by
John David Washington --

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.767
Danielle Brooks is Berniece.

00:05:03.767 --> 00:05:06.200
John David Washington wants
to sell the piano

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:09.400
to acquire some land
in Mississippi

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.567
that will change his life

00:05:11.567 --> 00:05:14.167
and keep him from going back
and forth through the, you know,

00:05:14.167 --> 00:05:17.334
the prison system or whatever's
going on down there.

00:05:17.334 --> 00:05:20.400
And she wants to keep it,
he wants to sell it, so,

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.234
that's the conundrum
of the play.

00:05:22.234 --> 00:05:24.567
-Yeah. And you actually played
in this --

00:05:24.567 --> 00:05:26.801
You were in this play --
-I was Boy Willie.

00:05:26.801 --> 00:05:28.133
I was the original Boy Willie,

00:05:28.133 --> 00:05:31.167
in the first production
at Yale, 30-some years ago.

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:32.033
[ Ohhs ]
-Wow!
-Yeah.

00:05:32.167 --> 00:05:33.901
-And look at you now.
-Yeah.

00:05:33.901 --> 00:05:35.133
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:05:35.133 --> 00:05:36.434
-Now I get the rest.

00:05:36.434 --> 00:05:37.968
-Now you work on Christmas, now.

00:05:37.968 --> 00:05:39.767
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.767 --> 00:05:41.400
-I get the rest and do nothing.

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:42.868
But I do have one question
for you

00:05:42.868 --> 00:05:45.334
before you kick me out of here.

00:05:45.334 --> 00:05:49.434
If I get a bill from Elon Musk
for $8, can I send that to you,

00:05:49.434 --> 00:05:51.334
since I joined Twitter
on this show?

00:05:51.334 --> 00:05:53.000
[ Ohhs ]

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.300
-That's right, you did.
-Remember that.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:56.234
My first tweet was on this show.

00:05:56.234 --> 00:05:57.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.601 --> 00:05:59.467
-I will get you $8.
I promise I'll get you $8.

00:05:59.467 --> 00:06:02.167
-$8 a month.
-Ooh!

00:06:02.167 --> 00:06:03.734
[ Laughter and applause ]
-Right?

00:06:03.734 --> 00:06:04.968
$8 a month, right?

00:06:04.968 --> 00:06:07.000
[ Cheering and applause ]
-We're going to talk --

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.701
We'll talk to you --
I'll talk to Elon.

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:09.968
-[ Laughs ]
-I'll figure out something.

00:06:09.968 --> 00:06:12.467
Samuel Jackson.
"The Piano Lesson" in playing

00:06:12.467 --> 00:06:16.100
now through January 29th
at the Barrymore Theatre.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:17.434
We're doing something fun
after the break.

00:06:17.434 --> 00:06:18.801
Stick around, everybody.
Come on.

